      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "But look closely. The rise isn't perfectly smooth. Aluminium is lower than magnesium. Aluminium's outer electron is the first one in a three p subshell, which is higher in energy than magnesium's three s, so it's easier to remove. And sulfur is slightly lower than phosphorus. Sulfur's fourth three p electron has to share an orbital with another electron. The two repel each other, so one of them is easier to remove. Exam answers say first ionisation energy generally increases across a period.",
