      "pronunciationText": "Lithium. Going down Group one, each element has an extra occupied shell, so the outer electron is further from the nucleus. The core charge stays at plus one, so the extra protons don't help. Further away means a weaker attraction, so less energy removes the electron. First ionisation energy falls from five hundred and twenty for lithium, to three hundred and seventy-six for caesium.",
