      "pronunciationText": "Now the second measure. In a covalent bond, two atoms share a pair of electrons. Electronegativity is how strongly an atom in a bond attracts that shared pair. Think of a tug of war, with the shared pair as the rope. The atom with the stronger pull draws the pair toward itself. Electronegativity has no units. It's a scale, called the Pauling scale, and fluorine is the strongest, at four point zero.",
