      "pronunciationText": "Electronegativity follows the same atomic structure. Across Period three, the core charge rises and the atoms shrink, so the pull on a shared pair gets stronger, from zero point nine for sodium to three point two for chlorine. Down Group seventeen, each extra shell puts the shared pair further from the nucleus, so the pull weakens, from four point zero for fluorine to two point seven for iodine. So the most electronegative elements sit at the top right of the table, and the least at the bottom left.",
